8275-f99d-57f5-8e70-446ed280a34f","instance--5ce206ee-baca-564d-9a84-366a24d29b98","instance--80ae483e-f333-55c4-92a5-c7cb09b3e0e7","instance--7e4450b3-96e6-5ea3-9044-166487cf8d11","instance--6877cc7c-ac0e-56a9-a122-7b5084c94683","instance--642d67e9-6057-57a0-8b38-c381727ab14f","instance--82a7df8c-77f3-5323-8895-69ca1c726c0a","instance--25703f68-458f-55bf-bf0b-8009313cf18e","instance--db7d915f-586d-51dd-a4d3-bd849efe5a65","instance--0e000c94-c22b-5569-b12c-f347f6c68cab","instance--b60588e6-1460-5b6b-a6f3-c9260663bea4","instance--be8bad0c-3b98-55e5-bbe7-8a57cce4980c","instance--ee4011d4-bdf3-5249-9330-3783722cf0a3","instance--7f866985-36ca-5550-8e8c-880f3f9914da","instance--08a75873-4a6c-5c69-92af-1534e02b2ef3","instance--156032f6-f1d8-5bd5-8c00-df47952066e8","instance--81898725-3bbf-5f8c-8811-589abab734a3","instance--009b2920-bca1-525e-a101-2b48737169d9","instance--fc7a0779-accd-5c6b-8654-be760cf806fd","instance--70861e10-84ca-5c6c-8ec9-26a267887094","instance--e713acbc-6c19-5b4c-aeec-4d5191adc148","instance--8d9f7ae1-15f5-52bd-bbc9-6e3195e1ad7b","instance--501b8975-6981-52d5-9a6a-c86381cc0272","instance--9b9f5a7d-b1ec-5c8d-99bd-a552226e3d68","instance--1cc9c2eb-3444-57ad-aa0a-9b64fff80a11","instance--fc06fed0-c14f-5a55-9ad1-b27e1804dc68","instance--de7d5665-53f2-5c7b-b695-5f2e6c70b2a3","instance--83955edb-b649-5084-9e3a-5f3819e9787e","instance--f9229ac4-701f-55d2-b0a2-63b08b381e69","instance--c6cee052-df97-53e1-ad46-90470a7b0352","instance--21f29fa3-b49c-5de8-a34c-47a12ccbe701","instance--f72e37bc-ac57-5eed-8583-40f5f928a545","instance--58c77bf4-d474-588b-8ff3-5ef3a6922d55","instance--47303066-23ee-5842-88c6-517782085683","instance--631cc5c0-926f-5fcf-a6e2-9089fac42973","instance--98a229c0-e210-52e3-9e55-9a41b54f26d3"],"properties":[["name","Qilin attack methods exposed through multiple cases"],["description","In 2025, Cisco Talos responded to multiple incidents related to Qilin ransomware. The overall attack flow is illustrated in Figure 5, and subsequent sections provide a detailed description of the tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) observed in each phase."],["scope","malware"],["author",[["name","Unknown"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","blog.talosintelligence.com"],["url","https://blog.talosintelligence.com/uncovering-qilin-attack-methods-exposed-through-multiple-cases/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Use leaked credentials for VPN access"],["description","Talos was unable to definitively identify a single, confirmed initial intrusion vector. However, in some cases, we assess with moderate confidence that attackers abused administrative credentials leaked on the dark web to gain VPN access, and may have also used Group Policy (AD GPO) changes enabling RDP to reach victim networks."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1078.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Attempt NTLM authentication to VPN"],["description","In the incident illustrated in Figure 6, Talos confirmed that credentials had been exposed on the dark web. Approximately two weeks later, numerous NTLM authentication attempts were made against the VPN, possibly using the leaked credentials. The resulted in a successful intrusion."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1110.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","RDP to domain controller and breached host"],["description","From the compromised VPN, the attackers performed RDP connections to the domain controller and the initially breached host."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1021.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Enumerate domain controllers and users"],["description","After gaining access to the victim\u2019s network, the threat actor executed nltest.exe and net.exe to enumerate domain controllers and collect domain user information."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1087.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Assess privileges and processes"],["description","In addition, traces indicate that the adversary attempted to assess user privilege levels through execution of the command, enumerated active processes such as explorer.exe via the tasklist command, and utilized the netscan tool for further reconnaissance."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1057"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Modify WDigest UseLogonCredential"],["description","The \"!light.bat batch\" file includes a reg add command that modifies the WDigest registry setting. By setting \"UseLogonCredential\" to 1, Windows is configured to retain plaintext logon credentials in memory at authentication, a behavior that can be exploited by credential-dumping tools such as Mimikatz to extract user passwords."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1112"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Run password recovery tools"],["description","After executing the reg add command, the batch file sequentially invoked netpass.exe, WebBrowserPassView.exe, BypassCredGuard.exe, SharpDecryptPwd, and ultimately Mimikatz. Within the script (see Figure 8), SharpDecryptPwd is configured to extract, redirect, and persist stored authentication data from multiple client applications \u2014 including WinSCP, Navicat, Xmanager, TeamViewer, FileZilla, Foxmail, TortoiseSVN, Google Chrome, RDCMan, and SunLogin, thereby consolidating harvested credentials for subsequent use or exfiltration."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1555"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Dump credentials with Mimikatz"],["description","Following the execution of SharpDecryptPwd, !light.bat launched Mimikatz. (Figure 9).\n\nCommands executed via Mimikatz targeted a range of sensitive data and system functions, including clearing Windows event logs, enabling SeDebugPrivilege, extracting saved passwords from Chrome\u2019s SQLite database, recovering credentials from previous logons, and harvesting credentials and configuration data related to RDP, SSH, and Citrix."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Stage stolen data into result.txt"],["description","pars.vbs formatted and consolidated the stolen data into a \u201cresult.txt\u201d file, which was subsequently exfiltrated to an attacker-controlled SMTP server (Figure 10). The script specifies the windows-1251 character encoding (Cyrillic), which may suggest the attacker or operator is from Eastern Europe or a Russian-speaking region."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1074.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Exfiltrate result.txt via SMTP"],["description","pars.vbs formatted and consolidated the stolen data into a \u201cresult.txt\u201d file, which was subsequently exfiltrated to an attacker-controlled SMTP server (Figure 10). The script specifies the windows-1251 character encoding (Cyrillic), which may suggest the attacker or operator is from Eastern Europe or a Russian-speaking region."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0010","technique":"T1048.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Archive data with WinRAR"],["description","Once collected, WinRAR packaged the targeted data, and in some cases the archives were exfiltrated using open-source software. Below are the actual arguments used to run WinRAR.exe. The WinRAR command is configured to exclude the base folder and to create the archive without recursively processing subdirectories."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1560.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f1e35721-7ac2-54fe-bcf6-5456d2faeaa3","120":"instance--3ff6777e-fcba-5b31-bf0f-3ddf77f6030d","150":"instance--cc6192f9-21a5-5d1a-b954-6a52d989b82d","180":"instance--62a87260-0181-5f49-bc05-733216e4d822","210":"instance--2f2d05c5-8e60-5ac2-b7af-e03027d67957","240":"instance--79c1ec18-d792-5d3d-a7bc-d94fe8b124cf","270":"instance--a035d357-e930-5d33-ab8d-d0314092d036","30":"instance--3af551b8-f6ac-5f54-9f6d-403fecdc69eb","300":"instance--298b5d2a-bf93-51e9-b052-19ce36114a5d","330":"instance--c8ea0da0-a19a-5766-b0d1-8524844a59d1","60":"instance--a204f87d-ace7-5a9e-b3d1-13202bdc5c7b","90":"instance--fff4de11-3f84-52c8-bb77-192210612a62"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--12","properties":[["name","Inspect sensitive files with local apps"],["description","Furthermore, Talos found that the attackers used mspaint.exe, notepad.exe, and iexplore.exe to open and inspect files while searching through numerous files for sensitive information."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cac05670-e90e-512c-99cc-c0adf909c3ef","120":"instance--43922820-ddd3-5742-a88d-49c20f8e3fd5","150":"instance--884271a6-8d7b-5c96-9ece-61be4126898b","180":"instance--373a94ef-653d-5c24-96f7-d0cf326d3aea","210":"instance--e58b782a-e75e-5141-bdf0-6d47dbed96bd","240":"instance--5960e46a-3307-5101-b96f-f1bae10e323d","270":"instance--a5ae1125-6ca5-54f1-b9d3-0091a0a38367","30":"instance--e7c521dd-fe09-528b-bb67-1ec53389b876","300":"instance--582e0864-cb5c-5de1-b6c0-e162ae91e8bc","330":"instance--3d5550f3-3e33-5d71-b71e-db2a0a957e5e","60":"instance--b83fc757-0bd4-5b63-a13e-e5b8ef5956d2","90":"instance--2a745819-837b-5585-a366-81a34117a6e5"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--13","properties":[["name","Exfiltrate to Backblaze with Cyberduck"],["description","In recent trends, the open-source software Cyberduck \u2014 which enables file transfers to cloud servers \u2014 has been widely abused in cases involving Qilin ransomware. By abusing legitimate cloud-based services for exfiltration, the attacker can obfuscate their activities within trusted domains and legitimate web traffic. As shown in Figure 12, the Cyberduck history file indicates that a Backblaze host was specified as the destination and that a custom setting for split/multipart uploads was enabled to transfer large files."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0010","technique":"T1567.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2accaaf8-d071-542e-9a10-06866a96b394","120":"instance--75ef5b2f-7c71-566e-baf2-29f54ced8138","150":"instance--73017f0a-a5f3-5dca-b91c-a2d37bcfe21b","180":"instance--2f1b6e5f-d3b0-59e5-b3c8-6c1399d1ce2a","210":"instance--c7aedd91-3346-5b75-9e3a-842851881a25","240":"instance--2146989b-d8a2-53f0-8a1c-cd3d976227e9","270":"instance--1b0bbd91-fa2a-5897-96d0-9e5918961c9c","30":"instance--e6b73353-364e-5586-a07b-e1fdc92ad2d3","300":"instance--0fdc5473-d5b9-5fed-91a3-21958da6287b","330":"instance--fd1cd9e0-5761-5725-801f-bf88b65914e8","60":"instance--a58b8357-6abc-58d7-ad2b-bec48fffcd9b","90":"instance--e8daf33f-0240-5544-9f99-3be7ac96fc1d"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--14","properties":[["name","Access multiple IPs and shares with stolen credentials"],["description","Using the stolen credentials described above, threat actor proceeds with privilege escalation and lateral movement. Talos has observed compromised accounts accessing multiple IP addresses and their network shares, as well as numerous NTLM authentication attempts against many VPN accounts , possibly using the leaked credentials."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1021.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--c80ca3ef-db0a-5372-968e-c17eb31a79ca","120":"instance--69989f45-927f-57be-92e5-5102fccd9f11","150":"instance--9b02c549-b183-5406-a100-249fb1868d16","180":"instance--c1d2a890-ed8d-5123-92d5-ceeaa937ee87","210":"instance--b785b7b9-02d5-5d04-be0c-0d02d4f85620","240":"instance--cde2d3fb-a23f-5188-9d7d-6c7f3cd3cebb","270":"instance--3fa59d94-25bb-5c51-af21-1a7c1fd91f66","30":"instance--fdd04191-1a03-5134-b88e-a55240471931","300":"instance--dddeb587-c160-5bdc-a385-f5d294f11e92","330":"instance--a13b6b46-2b8e-5660-b86f-03747a07fe24","60":"instance--d996db22-4d65-536a-83bf-a1db02b37136","90":"instance--258e2cac-1806-5147-8d61-a10d64a86e46"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--15","properties":[["name","Enable remote access via firewall and RDP changes"],["description","Additionally, to enable remote access they modify firewall settings, execute commands to change RDP settings via the registry, and perform related activities such as using rdpclip.exe and similar mechanisms."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1112"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--878d252f-de04-5857-ad0a-e8560794a9aa","120":"instance--bf65c103-2305-50be-8098-7718a8b010c5","150":"instance--348f71b8-78ee-5edf-accb-cd536c0db67d","180":"instance--e786d536-88e4-5ad4-8526-ae120c505f45","210":"instance--d3f3806c-3238-5b69-a0ca-334a1453e3dd","240":"instance--6dc42515-8e0a-5d8f-9dcb-cc6f0eb80f24","270":"instance--6a335c70-0c01-578c-9e01-614ace562750","30":"instance--c34e4c14-a710-535c-afd4-17d8ea759e88","300":"instance--60b19ce6-d4d3-5ce5-b2fe-3427fd0ea9a4","330":"instance--dea41a44-5c5a-520f-8975-25088fdd166c","60":"instance--e8f2f47b-1824-589b-af23-ab4291258936","90":"instance--67989025-38e3-56c8-b903-f474fc067511"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--16","properties":[["name","Add attacker account to local administrators"],["description","The following command adds a specific account designated by the attacker to the local administrators group. This grants them full control over the system."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1098"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--dbfe6415-cd2c-55f2-9509-06b6668ef23a","120":"instance--79ca45e2-afd7-51fa-9574-5085c7de4c84","150":"instance--39171cfe-3bf6-5200-b6f5-e97e3b047db7","180":"instance--8cda146b-7259-56b2-b337-56038a1f52d3","210":"instance--a662f8bf-2723-58c0-a1a8-9af9497cf428","240":"instance--a9b75b15-3be0-5e64-8132-40b87e7ae405","270":"instance--31896ecd-322b-5a41-bd1e-0b7a30b9d9d1","30":"instance--60868276-2726-597d-8f57-8aa7fc9c0738","300":"instance--4f5668fa-b6ef-57cc-93da-5cd1e1727a22","330":"instance--b022a562-9020-587c-a5be-97d254cc8f11","60":"instance--cf452b0f-192e-5357-ba8c-fbae1a6e4ae0","90":"instance--012cc6fc-0a37-5e6e-b9b7-07f3bcd2d02c"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--17","properties":[["name","Create full-control C$-style network share"],["description","They also run a command to create a network share named \"c\" that exposes the entire C: drive and assigns Full Control to the Everyone group, allowing unrestricted access and modification."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1021.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a73f63ad-1c10-59c2-82aa-bef4ae8f64e0","120":"instance--62757838-a58e-5d41-b7e3-1ccc64e8cdbf","150":"instance--3462202b-a91d-5325-abfe-876a63049484","180":"instance--72959cd4-5e05-5d69-a145-8b6f35720646","210":"instance--d3b85082-8de6-5ffd-8abe-c9e1ec43f533","240":"instance--0a22ffab-8bbc-55b1-85ec-df74e4a120f6","270":"instance--548b3ba1-955f-5e04-b6e8-064cc259e7a6","30":"instance--6f0a37c5-db81-5459-92c1-bc8ab8cd1fd3","300":"instance--e81be898-f7c2-56a0-a705-d2aba8831f75","330":"instance--8f207ed6-cb63-551c-9a40-583fac14fe80","60":"instance--8b44546f-f8e4-5d12-b172-99f9507395eb","90":"instance--f61db455-1665-504d-85b4-5fd5d40fbcc2"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--18","properties":[["name","Install remote management tools"],["description","The attacker installed software that was different from the legitimately used Remote Monitoring and Management (RMM) tools; this occurred before the ransomware was executed. While Talos cannot definitively conclude that the installed RMM was used for lateral movement, traces of multiple RMM tools were observed, including AnyDesk, Chrome Remote Desktop, Distant Desktop, GoToDesk, QuickAssist, and ScreenConnect."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1219"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--223a73a7-07a6-5688-bc70-e7fbf2c8afd4","120":"instance--2184e59f-b6bd-5ca7-8254-3872e152a964","150":"instance--eed82efc-7573-5ccf-97d8-e3f88a2337bb","180":"instance--453ded0c-8246-59f2-a14f-beca9e751cd6","210":"instance--143e4619-312d-5cbc-acc5-efed5f6c0164","240":"instance--659cf4a8-ca80-5204-8b8d-3240f6f370da","270":"instance--2dac3e32-a8df-582e-845a-3a7b1d510c1d","30":"instance--6ab42faa-5ba5-5c44-b387-40b1d021e500","300":"instance--96e5ad82-e4af-5995-8b69-6df7d7ce2490","330":"instance--a960fdd4-4889-5426-a406-4761d11be5ab","60":"instance--42df375f-d3e2-5d47-9faa-324aecbbf064","90":"instance--51395417-94d2-5b5a-881c-7b6cc63ade4e"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--19","properties":[["name","Connect ScreenConnect to C2"],["description","Figure 13 shows an excerpt of an actual ScreenConnect connection log, which indicates that ScreenConnect established a connection to the command and control(C2) server on port 8880."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1219"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--25dacfeb-3a3d-51fc-91b7-64ee405fe041","120":"instance--5a984174-ce49-510d-b6b6-d4f0e0ee332f","150":"instance--f2167f56-1cf9-5fea-a726-d003a591d391","180":"instance--70c47af3-1817-5ae2-9f6e-38421d85f808","210":"instance--cfd506cd-f673-5f4f-a5ff-5854ad8a39d5","240":"instance--b78e4cb3-2b2b-5706-8d59-d252dd134505","270":"instance--73410cfd-8533-5545-94b7-c06859fcd4a8","30":"instance--760fe684-ea1e-52a0-87e8-fa0bc5d62d70","300":"instance--fa30f213-64f3-55b5-85cd-9dbf46e0e8dc","330":"instance--0dbe5c9b-c2db-5139-a300-8054f3a8e205","60":"instance--a78137f8-a78e-563e-ad44-749594629166","90":"instance--626b6c26-479d-5895-a619-ee3dbb14136d"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--20","properties":[["name","Run obfuscated PowerShell to change security settings"],["description","Executing these commands makes three configuration changes. First, disabling AMSI prevents interference with execution of payloads such as batch files and malware. Second, disabling TLS certificate validation removes barriers to contacting malicious domains or C2 servers. Finally, enabling Restricted Admin causes RDP authentication to rely on NT hashes or Kerberos tickets rather than passwords. Although passwords are not retained, NT hashes remain on the system and can be abused by an attacker to impersonate the user."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--93ee4f51-8321-58fb-b05f-3a6fd3a6a8ab","120":"instance--02ee2d77-fc8c-55cc-8958-e3d0b5ead581","150":"instance--15aaf9f3-3996-5f9b-bee4-47f2963a0df4","180":"instance--1ae13e0a-be4e-5658-ba6d-c941c0d5cafb","210":"instance--87590098-5adb-5af7-aa75-039447d58b2b","240":"instance--87dee187-bf66-5b52-81e0-15b789ab6a7c","270":"instance--25c474c1-a795-5124-95ce-3e6163b067d2","30":"instance--ae371f09-8eae-53a7-a14c-34f9e72904fd","300":"instance--9ecc9c80-603d-5760-b2b6-f850dfd3eddf","330":"instance--b9543d3c-a7f9-50a6-b8a1-3fd4c6dddd56","60":"instance--cba1b44c-d7c9-5ebb-8433-b63b0b91427c","90":"instance--1c5f2ea2-c075-51ba-9f13-69b716c352cf"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--21","properties":[["name","Disable EDR with uninstall and service stopping"],["description","Talos observed traces of attempts to disable EDR using multiple methods. Broadly speaking, we have frequently observed commands that directly execute the EDR\u2019s \"uninstall.exe\" or attempt to stop services using the sc command."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1562.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--da12a10e-e9d8-58e0-9dda-e871f0fcaf7c","120":"instance--6e98f91f-940c-5b7d-8e4e-950f2c88b044","150":"instance--02b3e90f-a9f8-5908-b936-c779b2c570d8","180":"instance--5c256240-99ff-5907-aca7-0f81639a7419","210":"instance--e42c995a-6770-583f-9a60-afcdf41d5501","240":"instance--eee0e52c-22be-5b9b-819e-097b65b643d8","270":"instance--d4973194-aaba-5ce5-99ba-7d7c8bca7b50","30":"instance--91b449e9-d343-56d1-9376-8a2655b8032b","300":"instance--23579e20-df5a-5dad-9088-26b612c3c5aa","330":"instance--2ed64056-576c-519d-b8c7-4e1f2c06b6e9","60":"instance--c59d1168-f011-5687-803d-27aa797d72e2","90":"instance--321449b3-3e1e-5b4b-aab6-507e5ad1c36c"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--22","properties":[["name","Load dark.sys kernel driver"],["description","At the same time, attackers have also been observed running open-source tools such as and HRSword. The commands below are traces of dark-kill usage. Instead of running in normal user mode, dark.sys is specified as a driver loaded into the Windows kernel and the service is started under the name dark. The traces also show that, as needed, attackers re-register a driver from a different path and finally remove the service to erase their tracks."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1543.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--9f68185c-8d0f-5e34-b869-da9c17407e5d","120":"instance--99f65057-0748-5b22-b7a8-859b8cb9d46c","150":"instance--1c6c577b-3682-579f-9d80-c1a4c9632dd5","180":"instance--0372a821-a640-58c2-a8f9-f391b8fb0045","210":"instance--bd12903c-f92d-5416-a20f-eedd38d108f9","240":"instance--a221d4df-2c16-5e25-a121-f7cfbb303fb7","270":"instance--550d9be5-209a-50fa-99b8-4dfe7669b693","30":"instance--042db59c-d5d0-5002-ac74-85e947cc6579","300":"instance--2ce3cd55-fc34-5aac-8112-e6cc8fcd707a","330":"instance--55903f51-17c6-554e-8180-6f2511efa2b6","60":"instance--2b4af278-cf58-556d-9fa5-254ca76fcb98","90":"instance--a84c2c43-a2a5-5904-906d-da6a186887bd"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--23","properties":[["name","Elevate and launch HRSword via mshta"],["description","Additionally, to execute \"HRSword.exe\", attackers attempt to run a batch file with administrator privileges by using VBScript via mshta, specifying the runas option in ShellExecute. Because logs show that a shortcut file HRSword.lnk was created after 1. bat was executed, it is possible that HRSword.exe is being launched via that .lnk file."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1218.005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--08881caf-1468-53e2-baa3-c9da43e73b47","120":"instance--5344d679-b2e1-5528-bed5-6fe3fbc90036","150":"instance--f1a3ca80-d761-5917-981a-9d35e6a5161e","180":"instance--bb22e51a-29ce-531e-b80e-4a1d5343b453","210":"instance--380340c8-8f15-5075-a390-ac1b2706e43f","240":"instance--b8ca794c-8bea-5f4c-a746-ad3b31fd2d36","270":"instance--fb5c8b1f-7cc5-58a3-a457-0edfdefa168c","30":"instance--a124cc0a-728c-5b30-8b8b-2171584014e7","300":"instance--7d09cfe0-ac57-5093-a7ce-7c31042d3449","330":"instance--829e634f-5069-5370-8381-e0687a22b00e","60":"instance--0fbffc26-a516-5fcd-9fff-e9aee12c6467","90":"instance--96917b9c-4649-5345-82ac-b4e793881bfe"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--24","properties":[["name","Run Cobalt Strike loader"],["description","The Cobalt Strike loader Talos examined decrypts the encrypted payload contained in the .bss section of the binary shown in Figure 16, then deploys and executes the Cobalt Strike Beacon in memory."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1620"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6e9515e3-2497-5444-80ce-9466679d2504","120":"instance--25d30ffe-4a4f-53ec-a34d-de6cc58a2fb0","150":"instance--43abd457-ad7e-5db6-b146-d159a2936c52","180":"instance--f22410a7-1bbd-5943-9121-cf9edb5a0991","210":"instance--4a2a2f86-5543-5514-866c-4d5f4f5bcb3b","240":"instance--f2011b06-5138-5056-a1f2-0a96e9738966","270":"instance--a9d1b1c1-44f0-5281-b6b0-9133e0a433dd","30":"instance--c9339355-ad0b-5e98-9f42-ef0c11d380dd","300":"instance--dec744bc-b6ae-5258-bcb1-83f01a7bb747","330":"instance--54f63fd7-f831-5401-a04f-600f5e780c31","60":"instance--1dd30294-3434-540a-8b5f-d8bc1e3de794","90":"instance--e414165a-d829-5c22-ab74-6aa5e50c83d3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--25","properties":[["name","Execute decrypted Beacon via threadpool wait"],["description","In this code, the decrypted_buf is registered as the callback function via the arguments to CreateThreadpoolWait, creating a mechanism that will invoke this callback when the wait object becomes signaled. After that, execute permission is granted with VirtualProtect, and a MessageBoxA (shown in the figure and intended for anti-sandbox purposes) prompts for user interaction. When the user clicks OK, SetThreadpoolWait is called. Because EventA was created with an initial signaled state (bInitialState = 1), the decrypted code already mapped into memory runs immediately."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1055"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ce3f20b8-daf0-5682-a74a-dd9eb1251abb","120":"instance--08418575-7199-5323-8082-8e1d88a1ec11","150":"instance--15627176-59a5-5797-816e-a6cab3ea9da9","180":"instance--242a8d77-274b-5d18-ba35-771f6e0de836","210":"instance--d01bb126-419a-5d3b-a9cf-7b8df1d59112","240":"instance--0b76a14d-f362-5d5a-995f-2e318539789f","270":"instance--d534a23c-ea17-5a19-96f9-740e77b559a2","30":"instance--9b134899-2cf4-5fcd-9412-5363985ac68c","300":"instance--1bb6a59f-c750-5aca-a7c7-cecaf9c9f1f7","330":"instance--a346b253-e85b-53ff-8e33-33aaa8c928da","60":"instance--0c9baf75-2ba0-51ff-b084-c1044ff899fa","90":"instance--b86b5b84-3a18-51f2-b888-17161b8c5d47"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--26","properties":[["name","Use spoofed HTTPS C2 headers"],["description","The Cobalt Strike Beacon deployed in memory is configured (from its config) as Cobalt Strike version 4.x, with Malleable C2 used to spoof HTTP headers. In this configuration the http_get_header and http_post_header include \"Host: ocsp.verisign.com\", effectively separating the visible host header from the actual destination to make the traffic appear as OCSP or certificate distribution traffic. Communication is set to use HTTPS over TCP port 443 to the Team Server (C2)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--804d7975-bdc1-5371-a95e-4cff0aa0b8b1","120":"instance--aab4410b-5835-54c6-bc0f-d93b86440850","150":"instance--ad5c3f2a-3c32-5af5-9b9c-489a81eead21","180":"instance--3ff51605-dadf-546e-a273-07184c6549e2","210":"instance--9337c97e-ad0d-5d35-8b01-21c1e3f80296","240":"instance--49c4f7e6-8fe8-5919-bda8-039a2aaf3a61","270":"instance--4e395b92-9587-53cc-a957-cad25cc53df8","30":"instance--b917f3cb-7197-5ba7-8a3e-cbfda092d01a","300":"instance--ab650c26-b6f9-59ed-b26e-6f6ca03758dd","330":"instance--36c16e65-d9d7-519a-a8ae-a6dd521ddceb","60":"instance--0b7fc2fd-f6ca-532d-9f2b-ca34c65a881a","90":"instance--ff765750-9ba6-53a3-b366-8a863df1a603"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--27","properties":[["name","Distribute encryptor_1.exe with PsExec"],["description","Attackers sometimes run only a single encryptor, but Talos has also observed cases where two encryptor are deployed. In cases where two encryptor are executed, the first, encryptor_1.exe, was distributed across the environment using PsExec (see the command below). This command copies the local <encryptor_1>.exe to the remote \\\\IP address, elevates it to run with administrative privileges, and then launches it."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1569.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5788127e-30a2-5d63-8064-8a764c79ef88","120":"instance--50a9fb8c-a32c-508b-9ff8-6fbad48bdc18","150":"instance--fb5120ee-d53c-50d4-8806-fb538b7ace76","180":"instance--8c9e9207-faff-59a9-9ac0-4db98f799c06","210":"instance--17f4c1e8-e3de-51ca-a9b4-9407a08ef1f5","240":"instance--72709ae2-9e69-5094-89f4-3bb373306fff","270":"instance--4d10667a-8f14-5176-8d94-a90057c253eb","30":"instance--b7f4854d-0cc9-50b4-aae7-a9728bb18935","300":"instance--bb03752f-dd5c-5086-862e-11a1b554f970","330":"instance--ce6fbeb3-82f7-525d-94ba-6314c642da8e","60":"instance--5e319f8b-f917-5aca-9a32-bd424efd643f","90":"instance--923612bb-e746-52ea-b7f5-39eb0184150e"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--28","properties":[["name","Run encryptor_2.exe against network shares"],["description","The other, \"encryptor_2.exe\", is executed from a single system and targets multiple network shares."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--421e596f-663b-56b5-aacb-5c51f44887fb","120":"instance--54341936-f58d-5d7b-9140-0b8f37379212","150":"instance--6ca5d726-fab5-5c69-8490-e3c1002a1e49","180":"instance--00c7f913-8a5c-5e23-a21a-23f0b21c0795","210":"instance--c181f118-448c-5e8f-b83c-d03f6d177344","240":"instance--394b4c0e-56d4-5d48-8d37-2f9f3d5ea7f4","270":"instance--d6c97d2a-eacc-5edb-a7c6-1c3f45f4d771","30":"instance--35925ec4-d6e9-58b5-bd90-5e5a63a45b28","300":"instance--547b5bdf-80a3-54cc-b689-2eb517bfe68a","330":"instance--52fc9239-c76d-586d-b11b-ce234424de7d","60":"instance--ba71b506-6338-5b09-9d9e-61f0f5a2c6b4","90":"instance--a64014df-1f09-5b50-b208-7d398753c7cd"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--29","properties":[["name","Retrieve hostnames from Active Directory"],["description","A PowerShell command is being executed to efficiently retrieve the hostnames of all computers from Active Directory (AD)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1018"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0b4c0918-e86a-5085-87d7-f61b072e242c","120":"instance--12c9af38-e168-50fa-8765-64f02c0ebe95","150":"instance--c6746d99-565a-5e63-970e-a7aaa225ed30","180":"instance--e83416b9-e4c9-5e82-8828-e69fd027460e","210":"instance--de8a8abd-ceba-5797-84f1-54c1caa08458","240":"instance--72aee88b-434a-5ab5-8fd6-4eb52e953599","270":"instance--b36921b5-17c9-5a3f-a687-61f34c4b27cf","30":"instance--5ee548ea-d15e-5136-bc45-4995878b623e","300":"instance--992d0163-d34d-52e2-8eb5-14c76fe451e9","330":"instance--f718bcf2-a112-53c0-a88f-fa2d4cd342ef","60":"instance--35e08b82-20f6-565e-83cf-4b36a763a76d","90":"instance--ec521578-d320-599a-bd89-9ef7c991be84"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--30","properties":[["name","Install RSAT AD PowerShell module"],["description","Another PowerShell command observed is one that installs the Remote Server Administration Tools for AD (the RSAT-AD-PowerShell module). It runs PowerShell cmdlets related to Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) and Active Directory Lightweight Directory Services (AD LDS). This enables enumeration of domain users, groups, and privileges."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1087.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a94ae3bc-0276-54b9-858c-5463a38e5047","120":"instance--c8d6dba9-53d0-57c4-a2b1-9e203db4f4f4","150":"instance--27d385ee-53a4-5736-aabb-f1a1ed9ea255","180":"instance--4bf51010-637b-5f51-949b-001523c77066","210":"instance--09f04932-2a27-5832-a8e8-4610dda06af9","240":"instance--4f2d72ae-6d69-580f-8b0c-d4ae9d4de12f","270":"instance--9d7a47f3-e008-5167-aa95-d2f3028a2af7","30":"instance--8c32dfe1-51e3-5996-9ff5-4bf429a7d2e0","300":"instance--337f3c1a-0d8e-5224-bfbb-439cf9210776","330":"instance--9572f38f-66c8-57e1-9e25-eb2bccc50821","60":"instance--58bd39dc-d43a-589a-ab2c-770fca3958be","90":"instance--e5f57729-eb8b-5eb8-aded-8719ebfc59de"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--31","properties":[["name","Enumerate and clear event logs"],["description","Next, the command Get-WinEvent -ListLog * is used to enumerate all event logs on the system. Logs that contain records (where RecordCount is not 0) are filtered, and the .NET EventLogSession.GlobalSession.ClearLog() method is called to wipe them entirely."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1070.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f559716a-6c29-51f0-baf4-a78ada4c416f","120":"instance--3a99c30c-0974-5b88-947a-8d4d5018c15f","150":"instance--539cb708-7cef-5b47-9713-cf02a10dd28f","180":"instance--45b84d58-7b04-508c-95de-9c0a24c16baf","210":"instance--f378ed09-3ae8-59c3-8f51-7ee9f289ede2","240":"instance--dac8acc4-ae45-5a29-a802-f610aea4bb3d","270":"instance--d440b53c-203f-5d58-9232-58db096fec1b","30":"instance--5724a216-1fde-5009-a0b8-5e0e8304c406","300":"instance--4d4a2cda-784a-5b73-a4b1-9a347ad69d91","330":"instance--2645e09b-aa03-5922-95c7-83b80112d37b","60":"instance--f6e62445-6378-5cc6-9aa7-6e720e79c85c","90":"instance--50d2e1c9-6682-5564-bf02-588d6f5bd48a"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--32","properties":[["name","Disable HA and DRS in vCenter"],["description","As part of its PowerShell operation, it establishes a connection to the vCenter server, enumerates all datacenters and clusters within the vCenter environment, and disables HA and DRS in cluster configurations. (see Figure 21)"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1562.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6868cd06-be26-507a-926e-f64435403b14","120":"instance--728dd7d1-0a31-56e9-9255-ae2468760196","150":"instance--7c6f7608-f6d5-55f4-af98-7f5118111ce5","180":"instance--6a15bd20-ae2c-56f3-89f3-9613c7d0a53e","210":"instance--3a8617fe-4466-55ab-a31a-597fa4061f84","240":"instance--77d3fb4e-b647-5dc7-a530-a2f75999e7a0","270":"instance--c7e6acc7-9a0e-5d83-a134-f34e2326b148","30":"instance--1dc0e04c-d69b-510d-9ca3-5c5905e4b0fb","300":"instance--879c2341-1286-5fc6-8fe6-5cc85d411585","330":"instance--00d03d5a-5c88-50fd-9695-adb3d38eabaf","60":"instance--41351402-480e-5c99-80d3-6581eb23be1f","90":"instance--d7c1212b-8680-595f-ba56-2f67e709af5d"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--33","properties":[["name","Change ESXi root password and enable SSH"],["description","It then enumerates all ESXi hosts, changes the root password, and enables SSH access."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1098"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--d2b0af15-1a76-56b5-967e-83392d3a524e","120":"instance--8b244141-4595-51a9-b341-40a5bd6475f0","150":"instance--2bbee38b-99e0-58a8-a056-540067f44352","180":"instance--73e0c301-87de-52d2-b2e4-3d849eebdf0e","210":"instance--7802c0f7-7843-52d5-b007-3eff8c7d1131","240":"instance--d60b27ba-3372-54d2-a28b-22d8e3b5fa69","270":"instance--2e852633-0a31-5dfc-bff8-b9020f14ba6d","30":"instance--a9fbb487-8a29-5320-be7f-cc4f7fff7afe","300":"instance--5ebfb9d8-0128-5ed9-9c8e-2b4dccad2827","330":"instance--04b7316a-8435-5a70-8644-ca69aeb9e692","60":"instance--4ed526b2-9a5e-55e7-8455-6e4d4d38a74f","90":"instance--2c665158-422b-57c3-9252-9bf7660a2d73"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--34","properties":[["name","Upload and execute binary on ESXi hosts"],["description","Finally, it uploads an arbitrary binary to the \"/tmp\" directory and executes it across all identified hosts. It makes the binary executable with \"chmod +x\", sets \"/User/execInstalledOnly\" to 0 via the $esxiRights command (thereby allowing execution of unsigned binaries) , and then executes the payload on all hosts using the Process-ESXis function."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ea9a7792-7839-59ea-998d-ae1dea56a78d","120":"instance--c00ed3c2-6e11-5bad-a471-de1c5d5b1127","150":"instance--34b44527-55a3-5c92-8186-7acbcc5b0836","180":"instance--31085d73-dbd0-539b-a7eb-d0cf8c0ad149","210":"instance--41cb4329-d3cc-5d69-af17-ed081f51d1ab","240":"instance--a9746141-c99e-509a-84ec-2c7fc4f83c09","270":"instance--611e25a3-f62e-5dd0-96f3-35f034df05fa","30":"instance--ed84e6a1-b346-5536-8b6f-ff8172860a85","300":"instance--4cd527e8-26dc-5a84-b70f-26b862d8f563","330":"instance--81634646-9d4a-508d-af8c-0bbbe6816299","60":"instance--c0f244f4-3db0-5795-9786-be6a1dac7df8","90":"instance--53ccf17e-a618-5cee-9809-d3fdfdd5f0c7"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--35","properties":[["name","Enable remote symlink operations with fsutil"],["description","To broaden the scope of file access and increase the impact when ransomware is executed, the fsutil command is also run. This command performs operations on symbolic links; R2R means Remote to Remote (a network share to another network share), and R2L means Remote to Local (a network share to local). By executing these two commands and enabling each respectively, attackers can achieve different effects. for example, in R2R, a symbolic link on server A can be used to reference files on another server B; in R2L, if a shared symbolic link on server A points to a file on the host, an attacker can access the host\u2019s local file through that link. These commands may be executed using PsExec."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1222.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ce1eeea9-8f1d-573e-93af-afb7eb11aa69","120":"instance--b6595d5c-2c2a-573f-9d11-6fbdc82d35f3","150":"instance--7fd7f774-30f6-5509-af91-d92f117c1d83","180":"instance--2f3b18d2-e22e-5d1c-b551-b3a66f992fa5","210":"instance--83368dfc-1940-5b4b-a757-f748fde42ef2","240":"instance--a5ae3857-27e5-535e-a4d2-64e6add7c470","270":"instance--2761f5c1-1b34-5fb7-a06a-4e557a94a12a","30":"instance--d89915e5-6abd-57c4-8ad2-1bb4b59b3415","300":"instance--87bca308-74eb-551b-bf73-a5fb0243c5ff","330":"instance--edaf4323-f60b-5de7-bb34-69226e1950ac","60":"instance--5bc65240-ebfc-53e3-bcf2-9261c47cd3d5","90":"instance--b4c7e596-d037-5865-8936-023030612351"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--36","properties":[["name","Delete shadow copies"],["description","The ransomware changes the Volume Shadow Copy Service (VSS) startup type to Manual, and delete all shadow copies (volume snapshots) maintained by VSS."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1490"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2304431a-14a8-5b19-8875-dec47748456f","120":"instance--f7d91afc-dc3c-5cb5-acbb-0e32cce89f5a","150":"instance--119a9ab2-aee3-540e-9e5e-61ef53ccdd3c","180":"instance--37203ee9-6090-5e79-9837-d998b6b7bcdd","210":"instance--ae2148a7-02b6-5572-af26-6795a0663263","240":"instance--0ab23d41-9e28-569b-b539-94473810433b","270":"instance--4b643951-9695-5f55-b49e-de4d52e9fb8c","30":"instance--68c38407-773c-5468-8450-d4c5e50fc506","300":"instance--82c1929f-8462-52ff-beb6-6fb29652b887","330":"instance--0acf4fb4-711f-5aac-a483-cd67485f4dd7","60":"instance--7c7cc106-f525-509a-a681-4fe9659cfe20","90":"instance--6a87384e-8731-5c0e-8c29-1a843dbde3c6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--37","properties":[["name","Create ransom note in encrypted folders"],["description","The ransom note shown in Figure 23 is created in each encrypted folder. The note primarily states that data has been compromised, includes a link to a leak site on a .onion address that requires a Tor connection, and provides a URL (specified by IP address) that can be accessed without Tor for victims who do not have a Tor environment. It also lists the types of data included and warnings about the consequences of ignoring the demands."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cc6f5859-eb23-5f36-b96c-db2b0a780c18","120":"instance--440bc534-2a0c-5a64-ba90-7c35800f3f8f","150":"instance--64b5d529-45ca-53fc-a198-532e3f4effc0","180":"instance--0829e8b6-56bb-5cae-ba04-c6474a0b1be7","210":"instance--7dfa5d40-4162-59f7-bfe1-03b3241f926b","240":"instance--a4d1dcb1-63d7-5b87-a5a1-c9a4845784b5","270":"instance--c07879be-4e67-5922-a702-96e0f458cc94","30":"instance--eb2207fa-c658-56b4-ade7-719de3fdf7d7","300":"instance--f523814f-8bbe-5f16-9fe4-60737be2d4f9","330":"instance--d00f0842-45cd-5021-ace4-c6d047b7d21e","60":"instance--177a4f0d-3a9b-543f-90b7-935c7239d79c","90":"instance--979ca6e8-4039-5328-b2dc-12cf31687644"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--38","properties":[["name","Create QLOG execution logs"],["description","When running, it creates a QLOG folder in %TEMP% and multiple ThreadId({Number}).LOG files. They allow the attacker to inspect detailed logs of the encryption process."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1074.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f2f00bd8-d0c4-590d-a8b3-924ce7c0229c","120":"instance--bfeb3a2c-1dfe-510e-ab80-997e9da6d4f1","150":"instance--e2cd7725-c9d2-5e2b-b514-f86bbff1cece","180":"instance--61b632fc-2b4a-5e4b-9fe4-e2e4dd7726c2","210":"instance--3c95fc29-f44f-52dc-ae05-d43c2365da27","240":"instance--154d51ce-a412-50ba-b96a-3cb3130334b2","270":"instance--d70dba79-fefd-51d1-a957-f90ff37f3600","30":"instance--540038b1-d1aa-5c82-8398-8471cb7f49aa","300":"instance--19944388-a0b1-5a97-aa60-b7f972193bb7","330":"instance--1a6240fd-058c-5367-b54f-7af90856cf75","60":"instance--cf35a78b-621f-5168-9fb0-8ab9d16684ff","90":"instance--b62d3604-a5c4-58d0-a1dc-b8a4a3260d6c"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--39","properties":[["name","Set wallpaper image and registry values"],["description","The ransomware creates a JPG image under %TEMP% to be used as the wallpaper, and modifies the following registry values."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1112"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f6a34b46-cdad-58dc-b86a-f6cc9731b1b2","120":"instance--d66ef156-6f31-5081-822a-a9b1f163f537","150":"instance--8169b52c-57e1-59f8-9b29-27fa1eb798cb","180":"instance--89269a92-1c1a-52a9-aa85-6a7dd2e1e12f","210":"instance--ff756ba3-6dad-5b43-90c5-ffd261001013","240":"instance--412903a9-1501-5e86-ab14-ec0f77777f73","270":"instance--90e7dc0b-e519-5d22-9190-4a6d267c4f83","30":"instance--36f34756-c525-579d-acc1-18f9bcded829","300":"instance--4cb91a61-4889-58de-8bc2-a030a1930b38","330":"instance--a7521d08-9b55-526b-88fd-aa2c64708eda","60":"instance--20155536-1d6e-5e88-bfdd-4ed359c16327","90":"instance--fc8bf4f1-8aa9-5425-9767-7e1dd514c623"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--40","properties":[["name","Create TVInstallRestore scheduled task"],["description","After ransomware execution, the attacker achieves persistence through both task scheduling and registry modification. First, a scheduled task is created with the name \"TVInstallRestore\", configured to run at logon using the /SC ONLOGON argument. To disguise itself as a legitimate tool, the ransomware file is named \"TeamViewer_Host_Setup \u2013 <encryptor_2>.exe\", leveraging the TeamViewer brand (which had been installed as an RMM tool prior to compromise)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1053.005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--019a472c-57ac-551f-ba5f-aea06c9a7955","120":"instance--b68d41dd-cf9c-5287-9e02-fd1c68f80669","150":"instance--e29aa68f-2023-5bb8-a9af-92bd40bcf23b","180":"instance--07fcdaf6-6b4b-522b-98ee-9ed60c8f4b29","210":"instance--41f49756-7778-57a1-b86c-282bf5841259","240":"instance--8cfeb3ce-5d63-554f-bbe7-3f696ff90783","270":"instance--3d6b8627-a568-5405-be3c-afe6174fa045","30":"instance--fe0d6c9e-61ea-5c26-b835-304dd73cc8cb","300":"instance--c52dd4eb-5346-5c94-82e8-c0c7a6a3f8f2","330":"instance--35f11e63-48f8-5dc0-b402-23981e6ac5b1","60":"instance--81697adb-b4fd-558f-8b25-8e32f9a32b25","90":"instance--cd877f9d-700d-56e5-962f-862954f3bd60"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--41","properties":[["name","Add ransomware to RUN registry key"],["description","Second, to ensure the ransomware executes upon every reboot, its executable is added as a value under the RUN registry key.\n\nThis combination of scheduled tasks and registry entries allows the ransomware to maintain persistence across system restarts and user logons."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1547.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","Notably, the VPN implicated in this case had no multi-factor authentication (MFA) configured, which would allow an attacker with credentials unfettered access."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2ff8b105-17d8-5bc8-9736-a71ca9281068","120":"instance--fe9b11f7-9a07-51c8-93b2-02f34148833b","150":"instance--15f0676c-2f2f-58cf-99a3-b5eade2d286e","180":"instance--cdc5e3d9-a0b4-5995-98a3-d1a29532ffb1","210":"instance--75ed5df8-ff2f-5667-9748-b8587a1ee318","30":"instance--46009917-4258-54e5-9e91-c46c4a45d34d","330":"instance--54845373-a5f0-5af0-b348-5b0a3b4fbe67","60":"instance--f1f8d9a5-1f2a-55c4-af9a-f2629bc0827a","90":"instance--ddfb6e54-4af9-5771-910f-b4c7ba6e9860","branch:False":"instance--64607b7d-a4bd-56e7-9116-7bc21201c8bf","branch:True":"instance--f635d174-aa29-531f-b9c8-0cc481c6c1dd"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--2","properties":[["description","The resulted in a successful intrusion."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--64fa8274-9976-53b9-811c-a0e7e805b799","120":"instance--ce384754-4013-5515-ac17-4456e1d80bbb","150":"instance--99275651-db0d-57ec-a13c-6e557a4b9c7c","180":"instance--cbaa25ac-4f14-51f0-9962-f76fe36e7cd6","210":"instance--1c4fda5b-4605-5040-a88a-48f1df4144aa","30":"instance--39743932-1858-5655-a859-b27c0902b87a","330":"instance--c116df79-3c10-5931-96ec-25b4174ae13a","60":"instance--75b926aa-d189-5cd6-bc7b-5a947c88de41","90":"instance--4931e63d-9e52-5183-bbd8-7db1814b0f21","branch:False":"instance--fc00a7ae-0a9a-58b7-b24a-5def4ea9feab","branch:True":"instance--e3424864-637f-5b96-b87c-a8dcc22d8b9e"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--3","properties":[["description","When the user clicks OK, SetThreadpoolWait is called. Because EventA was created with an initial signaled state (bInitialState = 1), the decrypted code already mapped into memory runs immediately."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--253917f6-0fb3-5fc5-bd71-946fe7eb5b45","120":"instance--3f50f35e-a337-5d55-a037-5b923804b373","150":"instance--e1655f18-961e-5a7c-8605-a43fa92fe621","180":"instance--c536c45c-6edd-5cb6-8ee3-046111b98062","210":"instance--42f3c144-a229-5f85-b5be-d7f7668d557c","240":"instance--691fbaf3-af2f-5133-81cc-3f20013aafe4","270":"instance--2eab6914-e10b-5f1c-99af-5beccbf5d65b","30":"instance--ec3d9f12-fac6-5bd8-b657-4395a88ea91a","300":"instance--c4feed2f-8968-5ca9-9b2c-7d6dc36ae967","330":"instance--076ff030-b45a-5691-bef4-3f176aa05896","60":"instance--eb064d35-3662-50f2-819a-ebf3749e0b27","90":"instance--209d1071-226d-51fe-96d2-a60e78b0f246"},"id":"asset","instance":"attack-asset--1","properties":[["name","domain controller"],["description","From the compromised VPN, the attackers performed RDP connections to the domain controller and the initially breached host."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--e9a17326-5088-5d95-96d2-5e511bc26201","120":"instance--a11f392b-d04f-508a-a7fa